Lever: Sync overlap (steal report row 20). When a read connection's results for a group arrive, the next group is
encoded in the same pass, so the connection is never idle between groups. Base: 5a6ee6c (before the gather queue).

Measured (lv2 on t1, cap 3, 42,000 users, paired against HEAD in the same round, µs/request from monitor.sh):
  round 1: HEAD 246, sync 242 (sync ran under the per-cgroup perf counters: left out)
  round 2: HEAD 247, sync 242: total -5, PG -3; retired instructions +25k per request (1,223k -> 1,248k)
Not taken: no gain beyond noise, more instructions, and the gather queue (825c365) now drains at depth 1 on a clock,
which leaves no idle gap to fill.

